{"nodes": [{"id": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_ultra_adjudicator_reviewer_ultra_adjudicator", "label": "reviewer-ultra-adjudicator", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "user/.claude/agents/reviewer-ultra-adjudicator.md", "source_location": "frontmatter name: reviewer-ultra-adjudicator (model sonnet, effort high)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_ultra_adjudicator_adversarial_reconciliation", "label": "Adversarial pair reconciliation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "user/.claude/agents/reviewer-ultra-adjudicator.md", "source_location": "lines 35-92", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two reviewers examine the same lane on opposite assumptions, blind to each other, and a third produces the lane's single authoritative findings file \u2014 nothing downstream reads the halves. Resolution rules: both raised it, keep at the higher severity; only defence raised it, keep unless the code contradicts it; only prosecution raised it, decide against the code and the defence log \u2014 dismissed with a reason that holds means drop, dismissed with a reason that does not hold means keep, never reached means decide on the code alone. Every kept finding must be independently verified and its `evidence` set from the adjudicator's own check, because adjudicating from the two reports alone is arbitrating between summaries, which is how a confident wrong finding beats a hesitant right one. Severities are picked, never averaged, and no new finding may be smuggled in as an adjudication."}, {"id": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_ultra_adjudicator_dropped_list_as_calibration", "label": "The dropped list as pair calibration", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "user/.claude/agents/reviewer-ultra-adjudicator.md", "source_location": "lines 98-114", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The adjudication log's dropped list is the most useful thing the adjudicator produces: it is how the lead learns whether prosecution is running too hot or defence too quiet, and that ratio is the main signal to watch across runs. The log also carries a `coverage` verdict \u2014 both logs substantive, one thin, or both thin \u2014 so two silent reviewers with thin logs are reported as an uncovered lane rather than a clean one."}, {"id": "user__claude_skills_dev_loop_ultra_skill_dev_loop_ultra", "label": "dev-loop-ultra skill", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "user/.claude/agents/reviewer-ultra-adjudicator.md", "source_location": "referenced as the spawning skill for the adversarial trio", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_ultra_adjudicator_reviewer_ultra_adjudicator", "target": "user__claude_skills_dev_loop_ultra_skill_dev_loop_ultra", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "user/.claude/agents/reviewer-ultra-adjudicator.md", "source_location": "description lines 3-7", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_ultra_adjudicator_reviewer_ultra_adjudicator", "target": "user__claude_skills_dev_loop_ultra_opus_skill_dev_loop_ultra_opus", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "user/.claude/agents/reviewer-ultra-adjudicator.md", "source_location": "description lines 3-5 \u2014 \"the dev-loop-ultra skills\" (plural)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_ultra_adjudicator_reviewer_ultra_adjudicator", "target": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_architecture_read_only_enforcement", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "user/.claude/agents/reviewer-ultra-adjudicator.md", "source_location": "frontmatter lines 11-31", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "user__claude_agents_reviewer_ultra_a